 "description": "More describing words: pretty, quiet, famous — the な type.",
 "objectives": [
  "Use な-adjectives with な before nouns",
  "Predicate form with です",
  "Tell い- and な-adjectives apart"
 ],
 "study_guide": [
  {
   "heading": "な-adjectives take な before a noun",
   "body": "きれいな はな = a pretty flower, しずかな へや = a quiet room. The な appears only when the adjective sits directly before a noun."
  },
  {
   "heading": "With です, no な",
   "body": "このへやは しずかです = This room is quiet. No な before です. The な is only the 'glue' to a following noun."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Spotting the type",
   "body": "Most adjectives ending in い are い-type, BUT きれい and ゆうめい end in い yet are な-type. Learn those two as exceptions."
  }
 ],
 "examples": [
  {
   "ja": "しずかな まちです。",
